[2025-11-06 18:05:00 UTC]
REVIEW: Async Refactor Validation Addendum

KEY REGRESSIONS DETECTED:
  1. Event-loop lock binding
     • app/libs/framework_shells.py now instantiates AsyncLock() at import time (line 128) and stores it in _lock.
     • app/libs/framework_shells.py also creates _manager_lock = AsyncLock() (line 872) at import time.
     • app/libs/app_lifecycle.py does the same with _lock = asyncio.Lock() (line 9).
     Result: when the FastAPI/Uvicorn loop runs, using those locks raises RuntimeError("<Lock> is bound to a different event loop"), breaking manager and lifecycle APIs immediately.

  2. Awaiting non-coroutines
     • app/libs/framework_shells.py:603-612 – spawn_shell awaits self._active_shell_count(...), but _active_shell_count still returns an int. "int" objects are not awaitable, so shell startup fails before any process is spawned.

  3. Async file access misuse
     • app/extensions/apps/main.py:169-179 (and again around 198-215) calls `(await aiofiles.open(...).read())`, but aiofiles.open returns a coroutine context manager. Calling .read() before entering an async-with raises AttributeError (‘coroutine’ object has no attribute ‘read’). Shell log viewer crashes immediately.

  4. Supervisor cleanup disabled instead of ported
     • app/supervisor.py now comments out _cleanup_framework_shells() without providing an async equivalent, leaving orphan shells on shutdown.

OTHER NOTES:
  • app/main.py still imports ensure_app_running synchronously and calls get_running_apps() without awaiting. ensure_app_running/app_lifecycle are now async, so those callers either need awaiting or a synchronous adapter.
  • The new async FrameworkShellManager still calls self._active_shell_count (sync) from async context; either convert _active_shell_count to async or rebuild without awaiting it.

CONCLUSION:
The current async refactor does not run successfully. Core services fail at startup due to lock binding errors and unawaitables, and shell log viewing is broken. Supervisor cleanup regressed. Further fixes required before merging.

